  "Number": 27,
  "Question": "The points \\((2,-3),\\) \\((4,3),\\) and \\((5,\\frac{k}{2})\\) are on the same straight line. The value(s) of \\(k\\) is (are):",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(12\\)",
    "B": "\\(-12\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\pm12\\)",
    "D": "\\(12\\) or \\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(6\\) or \\(6\\frac23\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Points on the same nonvertical line have the same slope. Here the three horizontal coordinates are distinct, so the slope denominators are nonzero. The first two points give slope\n\\[\n\\frac{3-(-3)}{4-2}=3.\n\\]\nThe slope from \\((4,3)\\) to \\((5,k/2)\\) must also be \\(3\\), so\n\\[\n\\frac{k/2-3}{5-4}=3.\n\\]\nThus \\(k/2=6\\), giving the unique value \\(\\boxed{k=12}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
